          deepDive: "**V-た / V-なかった + ことにする** means *to treat something as having happened (or as not having happened)*: a deliberate fiction. The book: you change the facts to suit yourself (自分に都合のいいように事実を変えて言う), as in 犯行時間に一緒に飲んでいたことにしてくれ (*say we were out drinking together at the time of the crime*). The speaker knows the real facts but decides to present, record or behave as if they were different.\n\nConnection (the book): **V-た / V-なかった + ことにする**. The tense before ことにする is the whole point:\n- **V-る + ことにする** (N4) = *decide to do*: 来月から禁煙することにした (*I've decided to quit smoking next month*).\n- **V-た + ことにする** = *pretend that ~ happened*: ネットで調べたものを自分で書いたことにする (example ④, *pass off what I found online as my own writing*). V-ていた works too: 友達のうちで勉強していたことにして (practice 4, *claiming he'd been studying at a friend's house*).\n- **V-なかった + ことにする** = *pretend that ~ didn't happen*: 聞かなかったことにしたい (example ①, *I'd rather pretend I never heard that*); なかったことにする (*treat it as if it never existed*), e.g. withdrawing an offer — the story's 課長昇進の話はなかったことにする (*we'll act as if the promotion was never on the table*).\n\nTypical endings: **〜ことにしてくれ / 〜ことにしてくれる？ / 〜ことにしておいて** (asking someone to go along with it: 食事をおごる話はなかったことにしてくれる？ example ②), **〜ことにしよう**, and **〜ことにして、…** (a pretext, then what the person really did: 病気になったことにして、会社を休んで旅行に行った, Check 4). **その話はなかったことにしてください** is a set phrase for calling off a deal or offer.\n\nNuance: usually slightly negative — lies, cover-ups, excuses (examples ③④, practice 2–4) — but it can also be kind or face-saving: 聞かなかったことにするね (*I'll forget I heard that*).\n\nDon't confuse it with:\n- **〜ことになる** (N4): *it has been decided (by others or by circumstances)* — a real decision, not a fiction.\n- **〜つもり（だ）** (#120): 自分でやったつもり = you *believe* you did it (maybe wrongly); 自分でやったことにする = you *know* you didn't, and pretend.\n- **〜つもりで** (#59): 旅行に行ったつもりで (*as if you'd gone on the trip*) — make-believe to enjoy or motivate yourself, not deceiving anyone.\n- Other こと patterns in the book's ☞ p.221 list have unrelated meanings: **〜ことに** (#40, *to my ~*), **〜ことから** (#62, *because*), **〜ことだ** (#87, *you should*).\n\nJLPT tip: first decide whether the context is a real decision (→ V-る) or a pretense that contradicts the facts (→ V-た / V-なかった), then ask which version is the false one the person wants others to believe. In practice 1 the referee can't pretend he *didn't* see the foul (見なかった); in practice 2–4 the pretense is that it *did* happen (食べた, やった, 勉強していた). Review 問題2-2: お兄ちゃんが猫が割ったことにしてくれた (*my big brother made it look as though the cat broke it*). In listening 問題4-2 ①, 今の話、聞かなかったことにして asks for secrecy, so the fitting reply is じゃ、誰にも言わないよ (*OK, I won't tell anyone*).",
