          deepDive: "**〜あまり** (余り *excess*) = *so ~ that…, out of excessive ~*. The book: 非常に〜で、…の結果になった, mostly when the result is bad. An emotion or attitude goes beyond the normal and causes a result — usually unintended, uncontrolled, often unwelcome: crying, freezing, forgetting, losing weight, being unable to speak. The story: 恥ずかしさのあまり、逃げ出したくなった (*I was so embarrassed I wanted to run away*).\n\nConnection (the book): **V-る + あまり** (弟の病気を心配するあまり, example ①; 失敗を恐れるあまり, practice 4); **なA-な + あまり** (仕事熱心なあまり, ②); **N-の + あまり** (悲しみのあまり ③, 緊張のあまり, 驚きのあまり). The book's ＊ note: used with emotion words such as 心配・うれしさ・悲しさ・緊張. い-adjectives become nouns with **-さ**: 痛さのあまり (④), 忙しさのあまり, うれしさのあまり.\n\nRestrictions on the result clause:\n- It's a **fact** that came about, usually past: an uncontrolled or excessive reaction. Not a request, command or intention: ✗心配のあまり電話してください.\n- Deliberate, sensible actions sound odd: ✗驚きのあまり椅子に座ってテレビを見た (practice 1 → ✓持っていたコップを落としてしまった).\n- It must be the person's own reaction, not an unrelated fact: ✗緊張のあまり問題は非常に難しかった (practice 3 → ✓解答欄を間違えてしまった).\n- Positive emotions can also cause a reaction: 喜びのあまり抱き合って泣き出した (Check 3, *so overjoyed that they hugged and burst into tears*).\n\nRelated forms:\n- **あまりの + N + に**: あまりの暑さに倒れそうになった (*the heat was so extreme I nearly collapsed*).\n- **あまり〜ない** (*not very*) and **あまりに（も）** (*too, excessively*: あまりに現実離れしている, review 問題1-5) are other uses of the same word.\n\nCompare:\n- **〜ばかりに** (#48): *just because of ~ (with regret)*: 本当のことを言ったばかりに、彼を怒らせてしまった (*just because I told the truth, I made him angry*). The cause is a single act or fact, not an excess of feeling.\n- **〜てならない** (#121): describes the feeling itself (心配でならない); あまり describes what the feeling led to (心配のあまり食欲がなくなった).\n\nJLPT tip: questions often give two possible results — one uncontrolled or excessive (dropped the cup, forgot the anniversary, won't try anything new) and one deliberate or unrelated. Choose the first. Review 問題1-7: 興奮のあまりグラウンドに物を投げるファン (*fans so excited they throw things onto the field*) — 興奮することなく (#20, *without getting excited*), 興奮するどころか (#83, *far from getting excited*) and 興奮するからには (#18, *now that one is excited*) can't give the cause.",
